
<p>Lorenzo Franceschi-Bicchierai, reporting for TechCrunch:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>Almost four years after launching a security feature called
Lockdown Mode, Apple says it has yet to see a case where someone’s
device was hacked with these additional security protections
switched on.</p>

<p>“We are not aware of any successful mercenary spyware attacks
against a Lockdown Mode-enabled Apple device,” Apple spokesperson
Sarah O’Rourke told TechCrunch on Friday.</p>
</blockquote>

